    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section provides clinical implications emphasizing that caregivers' messages about eating, weight, and relationships affect daughters' body attitudes, attachment, and interoceptive trust, and it recommends therapist-led interventions to foster body appreciation. It suggests practical therapeutic strategies such as promoting realistic goals, focusing on body assets, encouraging supportive social environments, mindfulness of body needs, and using cognitive dissonance exercises to increase body appreciation.",
      "evidence_source": "\"Professionals can help caregivers understand that the messages they send to their daughter about eating, weight, and relationships are linked to how she feels about herself and her body and her ability to trust her body's internal signals.\"; \"Given the pivotal role of body appreciation in the model as well as the moderate-to-strong inverse link between discrepancy perfectionism and body appreciation, therapists are encouraged to incorporate interventions in their individual or group work to help women respect and appreciate their bodies via setting realistic achievable goals...\"",
      "warning": "None"
